                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "The CLI is literally one file.  I would prefer to keep it with the rest of the source files and not have folders with a single source file in them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/cli/meson.build",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "The intent in not doing linking the CLI with bmcweblib is that the CLI should not be sharing ANY code with the daemon.  Now obviously boost_asio.cpp breaks that (because the CLI needs boost to talk to dbus), but that should be its own dependency for the CLI and bmcwebd to link against"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/cli/meson.build",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Understood.\n\nI assume the cli would also become a large binary because of my patch.\n\nIt makes more sense now since you explained it.\n\nWill abandon this patch."
                }
